    "answer": {
      "short": "B.",
      "worked": "$100\\text{ g}=0.1\\text{ kg}$ and $500\\text{ g}=0.5\\text{ kg}$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{A: price per kg}&=\\frac{\\$0.40}{0.1}=\\$4.00/\\text{kg}\\\\\\text{B: price per kg}&=\\frac{\\$1.65}{0.5}=\\$3.30/\\text{kg}\\\\\\text{C: price per kg}&=\\frac{\\$3.50}{1}=\\$3.50/\\text{kg}\\\\\\text{D: price per kg}&=\\frac{\\$6.90}{2}=\\$3.45/\\text{kg}\\end{align*}$$\n\nB has the lowest price per kilogram, so it is the best buy.\n\nCorrect answer: B.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
